{
  "version": 1,
  "stage": "futuro",
  "order": 3,
  "title": "Futuro",
  "subtitle": "Say what will happen and what you plan to do",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "sl-futuro-01-domani",
      "title": "Domani",
      "outcome": "Say what you will do tomorrow, next week and next year with the futuro semplice.",
      "minutes": 7,
      "tense": "futuro",
      "grammarRefs": ["v2-a2-future-are", "v2-a2-future-ere-ire", "v2-a2-future-irregular"],
      "vocab": [
        { "it": "domani", "en": "tomorrow", "pos": "adv" },
        { "it": "prossimo", "en": "next", "pos": "adj" },
        { "it": "settimana", "en": "week", "pos": "noun" },
        { "it": "mare", "en": "sea; seaside", "pos": "noun" },
        { "it": "festa", "en": "party", "pos": "noun" },
        { "it": "presto", "en": "early; soon", "pos": "adv" }
      ],
      "activities": [
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-01-domani.1",
          "kind": "model",
          "prompt": "Who + will do + what + when",
          "body": "To talk about tomorrow, next week or next year, Italian changes the verb ending instead of adding a word like will: mangio becomes mangerò, vado becomes andrò.",
          "pattern": [
            { "role": "subject", "label": "who" },
            { "role": "verb", "label": "will do" },
            { "role": "object", "label": "what" },
            { "role": "extra", "label": "when" }
          ],
          "examples": [
            { "it": "Domani mangerò una pizza.", "en": "Tomorrow I will eat a pizza.", "roles": [["Domani", "extra"], ["mangerò", "verb"], ["una pizza.", "object"]] },
            { "it": "La settimana prossima andrai a Roma.", "en": "Next week you will go to Rome.", "roles": [["La settimana prossima", "extra"], ["andrai", "verb"], ["a Roma.", "object"]] },
            { "it": "L'anno prossimo saremo in Italia.", "en": "Next year we will be in Italy.", "roles": [["L'anno prossimo", "extra"], ["saremo", "verb"], ["in Italia.", "object"]] },
            { "it": "Marco farà una festa sabato.", "en": "Marco will have a party on Saturday.", "roles": [["Marco", "subject"], ["farà", "verb"], ["una festa", "object"], ["sabato.", "extra"]] }
          ],
          "tip": "Regular -are and -ere verbs take -erò, -erai, -erà, -eremo, -erete, -eranno (mangerò, prenderò); -ire verbs take -irò (dormirò). Four short stems to learn by heart: sarò (essere), avrò (avere), andrò (andare), farò (fare)."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-01-domani.2",
          "kind": "order",
          "prompt": "Build the sentence",
          "en": "Tomorrow I will eat a pizza.",
          "answer": "Domani mangerò una pizza.",
          "accepted": ["Mangerò una pizza domani."],
          "tokens": ["Domani", "mangerò", "una", "pizza."],
          "distractors": ["mangio"],
          "explanation": "Domani points to the future, so mangiare takes the future ending: mangerò, not mangio.",
          "hint": "Start with when."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-01-domani.3",
          "kind": "cloze",
          "prompt": "Finish the sentence",
          "template": "La settimana prossima ____ a Roma.",
          "en": "Next week you will go to Rome.",
          "blanks": [
            {
              "accept": ["andrai"],
              "options": ["andrai", "andrò", "andremo"],
              "bank": ["andranno", "andrete"],
              "free": false,
              "slot": null,
              "explanation": "tu takes andrai: the future of andare is andr- plus -ai."
            }
          ],
          "hint": "The subject is tu (you)."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-01-domani.4",
          "kind": "order",
          "prompt": "Build the sentence",
          "en": "Next year we will be in Italy.",
          "answer": "L'anno prossimo saremo in Italia.",
          "accepted": [],
          "tokens": ["L'anno", "prossimo", "saremo", "in", "Italia."],
          "distractors": ["sarò", "sarete"],
          "explanation": "noi takes saremo, the future of essere; sarò is io and sarete is voi.",
          "hint": "When comes first here."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-01-domani.5",
          "kind": "cloze",
          "prompt": "Say what you will do",
          "template": "Domani sera ____ un film con Anna.",
          "en": "Tomorrow evening I will watch a film with Anna.",
          "blanks": [
            {
              "accept": ["guarderò", "vedrò"],
              "options": ["guarderò", "vedrò", "guarderai", "guarderanno"],
              "bank": ["vedrai", "guarderemo"],
              "free": true,
              "slot": { "pos": "verb", "person": 0, "tense": "futuro" },
              "explanation": "io takes -ò in the future: guarderò (guardare) or vedrò (vedere)."
            }
          ],
          "hint": "Pick a form, or type any verb in the future for io."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-01-domani.6",
          "kind": "dialogue",
          "prompt": "Plans for tomorrow",
          "partner": "Sara",
          "turns": [
            { "speaker": "partner", "it": "Ciao! Che cosa farai domani?", "en": "Hi! What will you do tomorrow?" },
            {
              "speaker": "you",
              "template": "Domani ____ al mare.",
              "en": "Tomorrow I will go to the sea.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "accept": ["andrò"],
                  "options": ["andrò", "andrai", "andranno"],
                  "bank": ["andremo"],
                  "free": false,
                  "slot": null,
                  "explanation": "io takes andrò."
                }
              ],
              "reactions": [
                { "when": ["andrò"], "it": "Che bello! Con chi andrai?", "en": "How nice! Who will you go with?" },
                { "when": "*", "it": "Capito.", "en": "Got it." }
              ]
            },
            { "speaker": "partner", "it": "E la settimana prossima che cosa farai?", "en": "And what will you do next week?" },
            {
              "speaker": "you",
              "template": "La settimana prossima ____ molto.",
              "en": "Next week I will ____ a lot.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "accept": ["lavorerò", "studierò"],
                  "options": ["lavorerò", "studierò", "lavorerai"],
                  "bank": ["lavorerà", "studieremo"],
                  "free": true,
                  "slot": { "pos": "verb", "person": 0, "tense": "futuro" },
                  "explanation": "The future for io ends in -ò: lavorerò, studierò."
                }
              ],
              "reactions": [
                { "when": ["lavorerò"], "it": "Che peccato! Lavorerai anche sabato?", "en": "What a pity! Will you work on Saturday too?" },
                { "when": ["studierò"], "it": "Hai un esame? In bocca al lupo!", "en": "Do you have an exam? Good luck!" },
                { "when": "*", "it": "Capisco. Allora ci vediamo domenica!", "en": "I see. Then see you on Sunday!" }
              ]
            },
            { "speaker": "partner", "it": "Allora buona settimana! Ciao!", "en": "Then have a good week! Bye!" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-01-domani.7",
          "kind": "cloze",
          "prompt": "Two futures, one subject",
          "template": "Sabato Marco ____ una festa e ____ tutti gli amici.",
          "en": "On Saturday Marco will have a party and will invite all his friends.",
          "blanks": [
            {
              "accept": ["farà"],
              "options": ["farà", "farò", "fanno"],
              "bank": ["faremo"],
              "free": false,
              "slot": null,
              "explanation": "Marco is lui: farà."
            },
            {
              "accept": ["inviterà"],
              "options": ["inviterà", "inviterai", "inviteremo"],
              "bank": ["invita"],
              "free": false,
              "slot": null,
              "explanation": "Same subject, same ending: inviterà."
            }
          ],
          "hint": "Both verbs talk about Marco."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-01-domani.8",
          "kind": "build",
          "prompt": "Say it yourself",
          "tense": "futuro",
          "roles": [
            {
              "role": "subject",
              "items": [
                { "it": "Io", "en": "I", "person": 0 },
                { "it": "Tu", "en": "you", "person": 1 },
                { "it": "Mia sorella", "en": "my sister", "person": 2, "gender": "f" },
                { "it": "Noi", "en": "we", "person": 3 },
                { "it": "I miei amici", "en": "my friends", "person": 5, "gender": "m" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "role": "verb",
              "items": [
                { "inf": "mangiare", "en": "eat" },
                { "inf": "comprare", "en": "buy" },
                { "inf": "fare", "en": "make" },
                { "inf": "vedere", "en": "see" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "role": "object",
              "learned": { "pos": "noun", "category": ["food", "arts"], "article": "definite" },
              "items": [
                { "it": "una pizza", "en": "a pizza" },
                { "it": "un gelato", "en": "an ice cream" },
                { "it": "una torta", "en": "a cake" },
                { "it": "un film", "en": "a film" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "role": "extra",
              "optional": true,
              "items": [
                { "it": "domani", "en": "tomorrow" },
                { "it": "la settimana prossima", "en": "next week" },
                { "it": "l'anno prossimo", "en": "next year" },
                { "it": "sabato", "en": "on Saturday" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "examples": [
            "Io mangerò una pizza domani.",
            "Mia sorella farà una torta sabato.",
            "I miei amici vedranno un film la settimana prossima."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sl-futuro-02-progetti",
      "title": "Progetti",
      "outcome": "Talk about plans with volere, dovere and potere plus an infinitive, with andare a, and with the present used for a fixed plan.",
      "minutes": 7,
      "tense": "presente",
      "grammarRefs": ["v2-a2-near-plan", "v2-a1-want-need", "v2-a1-potere-requests"],
      "vocab": [
        { "it": "progetto", "en": "project; plan", "pos": "noun" },
        { "it": "vacanza", "en": "holiday", "pos": "noun" },
        { "it": "fine settimana", "en": "weekend", "pos": "noun" },
        { "it": "esame", "en": "exam", "pos": "noun" },
        { "it": "albergo", "en": "hotel", "pos": "noun" },
        { "it": "stasera", "en": "this evening; tonight", "pos": "adv" }
      ],
      "activities": [
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-02-progetti.1",
          "kind": "model",
          "prompt": "Who + wants / has to / can + do what",
          "body": "A plan often needs two verbs: a modal (voglio, devo, posso) or andare a, then the infinitive. When the plan is already fixed, the present is enough: Domani vado al mare.",
          "pattern": [
            { "role": "subject", "label": "who" },
            { "role": "verb", "label": "wants / must / can" },
            { "role": "object", "label": "to do what" },
            { "role": "extra", "label": "when" }
          ],
          "examples": [
            { "it": "Domani voglio andare al mare.", "en": "Tomorrow I want to go to the sea.", "roles": [["Domani", "extra"], ["voglio", "verb"], ["andare al mare.", "object"]] },
            { "it": "La settimana prossima devo lavorare.", "en": "Next week I have to work.", "roles": [["La settimana prossima", "extra"], ["devo", "verb"], ["lavorare.", "object"]] },
            { "it": "Stasera andiamo a mangiare una pizza.", "en": "Tonight we are going to eat a pizza.", "roles": [["Stasera", "extra"], ["andiamo a", "verb"], ["mangiare una pizza.", "object"]] },
            { "it": "Domani vado al mare.", "en": "Tomorrow I am going to the sea.", "roles": [["Domani", "extra"], ["vado", "verb"], ["al mare.", "object"]] }
          ],
          "tip": "Volere, dovere and potere are irregular in the present: voglio, devo, posso; vogliamo, dobbiamo, possiamo. The verb after them never changes: devo lavorare, dobbiamo lavorare."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-02-progetti.2",
          "kind": "order",
          "prompt": "Build the sentence",
          "en": "Tomorrow I want to go to the sea.",
          "answer": "Domani voglio andare al mare.",
          "accepted": ["Voglio andare al mare domani."],
          "tokens": ["Domani", "voglio", "andare", "al", "mare."],
          "distractors": ["vuole"],
          "explanation": "io takes voglio; the second verb stays in the infinitive: andare.",
          "hint": "When, then who wants, then what."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-02-progetti.3",
          "kind": "cloze",
          "prompt": "Finish the sentence",
          "template": "Sabato ____ studiare per l'esame.",
          "en": "On Saturday I have to study for the exam.",
          "blanks": [
            {
              "accept": ["devo"],
              "options": ["devo", "deve", "devi"],
              "bank": ["dobbiamo", "dovete"],
              "free": false,
              "slot": null,
              "explanation": "io takes devo: I have to."
            }
          ],
          "hint": "Who has to study? I do."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-02-progetti.4",
          "kind": "cloze",
          "prompt": "Going to do something",
          "template": "Stasera ____ a mangiare una pizza con gli amici.",
          "en": "Tonight we are going to eat a pizza with friends.",
          "blanks": [
            {
              "accept": ["andiamo"],
              "options": ["andiamo", "andare", "vado"],
              "bank": ["andate"],
              "free": false,
              "slot": null,
              "explanation": "noi takes andiamo; andare a plus an infinitive says what you are going to do."
            }
          ],
          "hint": "The subject is noi (we)."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-02-progetti.5",
          "kind": "dialogue",
          "prompt": "This weekend",
          "partner": "Luca",
          "turns": [
            { "speaker": "partner", "it": "Ciao! Che cosa fai questo fine settimana?", "en": "Hi! What are you doing this weekend?" },
            {
              "speaker": "you",
              "template": "Sabato ____ al cinema.",
              "en": "On Saturday I am going to the cinema.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "accept": ["vado"],
                  "options": ["vado", "andare", "vai"],
                  "bank": ["va"],
                  "free": false,
                  "slot": null,
                  "explanation": "A fixed plan takes the present: vado. The infinitive andare needs a modal before it."
                }
              ],
              "reactions": [
                { "when": ["vado"], "it": "Bello! Che film vuoi vedere?", "en": "Nice! What film do you want to see?" },
                { "when": "*", "it": "Va bene.", "en": "All right." }
              ]
            },
            { "speaker": "partner", "it": "E domenica?", "en": "And on Sunday?" },
            {
              "speaker": "you",
              "template": "Domenica devo ____.",
              "en": "On Sunday I have to ____.",
              "blanks": [
                {
                  "accept": ["lavorare", "studiare", "pulire la casa"],
                  "options": ["lavorare", "studiare", "pulire la casa"],
                  "bank": [],
                  "free": false,
                  "slot": null,
                  "explanation": "After devo the verb stays in the infinitive."
                }
              ],
              "reactions": [
                { "when": ["lavorare"], "it": "Di domenica? Che peccato!", "en": "On a Sunday? What a pity!" },
                { "when": ["studiare"], "it": "Hai un esame? In bocca al lupo!", "en": "Do you have an exam? Good luck!" },
                { "when": "*", "it": "Capisco. Allora ci vediamo la settimana prossima!", "en": "I see. Then see you next week!" }
              ]
            },
            { "speaker": "partner", "it": "Va bene, buon fine settimana!", "en": "All right, have a good weekend!" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-02-progetti.6",
          "kind": "order",
          "prompt": "Build the sentence",
          "en": "Next week we can book the hotel.",
          "answer": "La settimana prossima possiamo prenotare l'albergo.",
          "accepted": ["Possiamo prenotare l'albergo la settimana prossima."],
          "tokens": ["La", "settimana", "prossima", "possiamo", "prenotare", "l'albergo."],
          "distractors": ["possono"],
          "explanation": "noi takes possiamo, then the infinitive prenotare.",
          "hint": "Start with when."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-02-progetti.7",
          "kind": "cloze",
          "prompt": "Wants and limits",
          "template": "Quest'estate ____ andare in vacanza, ma non ____ spendere molto.",
          "en": "This summer we want to go on holiday, but we can't spend much.",
          "blanks": [
            {
              "accept": ["vogliamo"],
              "options": ["vogliamo", "voglio", "vuole"],
              "bank": ["volete"],
              "free": false,
              "slot": null,
              "explanation": "noi takes vogliamo."
            },
            {
              "accept": ["possiamo"],
              "options": ["possiamo", "posso", "potete"],
              "bank": ["possono"],
              "free": false,
              "slot": null,
              "explanation": "noi takes possiamo; non possiamo means we can't."
            }
          ],
          "hint": "Both verbs are about noi (we)."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-02-progetti.8",
          "kind": "build",
          "prompt": "Say it yourself",
          "tense": "presente",
          "roles": [
            {
              "role": "subject",
              "items": [
                { "it": "Io", "en": "I", "person": 0 },
                { "it": "Tu", "en": "you", "person": 1 },
                { "it": "Mia madre", "en": "my mother", "person": 2, "gender": "f" },
                { "it": "Noi", "en": "we", "person": 3 },
                { "it": "I miei amici", "en": "my friends", "person": 5, "gender": "m" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "role": "verb",
              "items": [
                { "inf": "volere", "en": "want to" },
                { "inf": "dovere", "en": "have to" },
                { "inf": "potere", "en": "be able to" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "role": "object",
              "items": [
                { "it": "andare al mare", "en": "go to the sea" },
                { "it": "lavorare", "en": "work" },
                { "it": "studiare l'italiano", "en": "study Italian" },
                { "it": "visitare Roma", "en": "visit Rome" },
                { "it": "fare una festa", "en": "have a party" }
              ]
            },
            {
              "role": "extra",
              "optional": true,
              "items": [
                { "it": "domani", "en": "tomorrow" },
                { "it": "sabato", "en": "on Saturday" },
                { "it": "la settimana prossima", "en": "next week" },
                { "it": "quest'estate", "en": "this summer" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "examples": [
            "Io voglio andare al mare domani.",
            "Noi dobbiamo lavorare sabato.",
            "Mia madre può visitare Roma la settimana prossima."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sl-futuro-03-se",
      "title": "Se…",
      "outcome": "Link a condition in the present to a result in the present or the future with se.",
      "minutes": 7,
      "tense": "futuro",
      "grammarRefs": ["v2-a2-real-if", "v2-b1-real-condition"],
      "vocab": [
        { "it": "bel tempo", "en": "good weather", "pos": "expr" },
        { "it": "sole", "en": "sun", "pos": "noun" },
        { "it": "montagna", "en": "mountain", "pos": "noun" },
        { "it": "insieme", "en": "together", "pos": "adv" },
        { "it": "soldi", "en": "money", "pos": "noun" },
        { "it": "macchina", "en": "car", "pos": "noun" }
      ],
      "activities": [
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-03-se.1",
          "kind": "model",
          "prompt": "If + condition, + result",
          "body": "Se introduces a condition. After se the verb is in the present (se piove); the result can be in the present (resto a casa) or in the future (resterò a casa).",
          "pattern": [
            { "role": "link", "label": "if" },
            { "role": "extra", "label": "condition (present)" },
            { "role": "verb", "label": "result" },
            { "role": "object", "label": "what / where" }
          ],
          "examples": [
            { "it": "Se piove, resto a casa.", "en": "If it rains, I stay at home.", "roles": [["Se", "link"], ["piove,", "extra"], ["resto", "verb"], ["a casa.", "object"]] },
            { "it": "Se hai tempo, andremo al cinema.", "en": "If you have time, we will go to the cinema.", "roles": [["Se", "link"], ["hai tempo,", "extra"], ["andremo", "verb"], ["al cinema.", "object"]] },
            { "it": "Se fa bel tempo, andrò al mare.", "en": "If the weather is nice, I will go to the sea.", "roles": [["Se", "link"], ["fa bel tempo,", "extra"], ["andrò", "verb"], ["al mare.", "object"]] },
            { "it": "Se studi, passerai l'esame.", "en": "If you study, you will pass the exam.", "roles": [["Se", "link"], ["studi,", "extra"], ["passerai", "verb"], ["l'esame.", "object"]] }
          ],
          "tip": "Keep the present after se: se piove, se hai tempo. A comma separates the condition from the result, and the order can flip: Resto a casa se piove."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-03-se.2",
          "kind": "order",
          "prompt": "Build the sentence",
          "en": "If it rains, I stay at home.",
          "answer": "Se piove, resto a casa.",
          "accepted": [],
          "tokens": ["Se", "piove,", "resto", "a", "casa."],
          "distractors": ["resterai"],
          "explanation": "The condition se piove is in the present; the result resto matches io.",
          "hint": "Start with se."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-03-se.3",
          "kind": "cloze",
          "prompt": "Finish the sentence",
          "template": "Se hai tempo, ____ al cinema insieme.",
          "en": "If you have time, we will go to the cinema together.",
          "blanks": [
            {
              "accept": ["andremo"],
              "options": ["andremo", "andrai", "andranno"],
              "bank": ["andrete"],
              "free": false,
              "slot": null,
              "explanation": "noi takes andremo: the result is in the future."
            }
          ],
          "hint": "Insieme tells you the subject is noi."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-03-se.4",
          "kind": "cloze",
          "prompt": "Say what you will do",
          "template": "Se fa bel tempo, domenica ____ al mare.",
          "en": "If the weather is nice, on Sunday I will go to the sea.",
          "blanks": [
            {
              "accept": ["andrò"],
              "options": ["andrò", "andrai", "andranno"],
              "bank": ["andremo"],
              "free": true,
              "slot": { "pos": "verb", "person": 0, "tense": "futuro" },
              "explanation": "io takes andrò."
            }
          ],
          "hint": "Or type another verb in the future for io, like resterò or tornerò."
        },
        {
          "id": "sl-futuro-03-se.5",
          "kind": "dialogue",
          "prompt": "Sunday plans",
